   "install": {
    "title": "Quick start",
    "html": "<p>With Docker installed, run:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">docker run -d \\\n  --name memos \\\n  -p 5230:5230 \\\n  -v ~/.memos:/var/opt/memos \\\n  neosmemo/memos:stable\n</code></pre>\n<p>Open <a href=\"http://localhost:5230\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">http://localhost:5230</a> and create the first account. Everything Memos keeps is in <code>~/.memos</code>, so back up that one folder.</p>\n<p>Other ways to run Memos, including Docker Compose, Kubernetes, and a plain binary, are in the <a href=\"https://usememos.com/docs/deploy\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">deployment guide</a>.</p>",
